{"id":132731,"title":"Diffusion and multiple anisotropic scattering for global illumination in clouds","url":"https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1410406/?q=multiple scattering rendering","final_url":"https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1410406/m2/1/high_res_d/15014347.pdf","year":null,"kind":"link","source":"os:digital.library.unt.edu","doi":null,"arxiv":null,"sha256":"95cdcbe4dc1ed63a8019c8da1499cd266c11bb1c8673c2a08f980c2af7f119c6","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"url","fetched_at":1793306574.7860951,"text_chars":34210,"abstract":"The diffusion method is a good approximation inside the dense core of a cloud, but not at the more tenuous boundary regions. Also, it breaks down in regions where the density of scattering droplets is zero. We have enhanced it by using hardware cell projection volume rendering at cloud border voxels to account for the straight line light transport across these empty regions. We have also used this hardware volume rendering at key voxels in the low-density boundary regions to account for the multiple anisotropic scattering of the environment.","file":null,"marks":["unofficial"],"links":["https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1410406/m2/1/high_res_d/15014347.pdf","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1410406/?q=multiple scattering rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1410406/?q=single scattering volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1410406/?q=henyey-greenstein phase function","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1410406/?q=voxel global illumination","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1410406/?q=diffuse global illumination sky sampling","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1410406/?q=global cloud flow","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1410406/?q=nishita sky model","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1410406/?q=octree multiple scattering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1410406/?q=hardware ray tracing global illumination","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1410406/?q=point-based global illumination participating media","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1410406/?q=precomputed single scattering"],"cited_by":[{"path":"5616-hardware-accelerated-volume-rendering.md","name":"Hardware-Accelerated Volume Rendering","k":6},{"path":"35-single-and-multiple-scattering.md","name":"Single and multiple scattering","k":5},{"path":"9989-hierarchical-volume-rendering-for-cloud-surface.md","name":"Hierarchical Volume Rendering for Cloud Surface","k":1},{"path":"10010-hierarchical-viewing-cube-sampling.md","name":"Hierarchical Viewing Cube Sampling","k":1},{"path":"9971-diffusion-approximation-for-cloud-radiance.md","name":"Diffusion Approximation for Cloud Radiance","k":1},{"path":"9992-final-composition.md","name":"Final Composition","k":2}]}